</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>O loving wisdom of our God,</l><l>When all was sin and shame,</l><l>He, the last Adam, to the fight</l><l>And to the rescue came.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>O wisest love! that flesh and blood</l><l>Which did in Adam fail,</l><l>Should strive afresh against the foe,</l><l>Should strive and should prevail.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>And that a higher gift than grace</l><l>Should flesh and blood refine,</l><l>God’s presence, and His very self</l><l>And essence all-divine.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>O generous love! that He, who smote</l><l>In man for man the foe,</l><l>The double agony in man</l><l>For man should undergo.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>And in the garden secretly,</l><l>And on the cross on high,</l><l>Should teach His brethren, and inspire</l><l>To suffer and to die.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Praise to the Holiest in the height,</l><l>And in the depth be praise:</l><l>In all His words most wonderful;</l><l>Most sure in all His ways.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
